<!--
purpose: Canonical skeleton for the `govtech-foia-ba-pack` artefact — one section per rule in content/01-core-rules.xml.
consumes: Data model, store list, schedule authority, contract clauses, launch plan, and the two officers' sign-off.
produces: A committed pack at .product/govtech-foia-ba-pack/<system>.md plus its JSON form validated by scripts/validate-govtech-foia-ba-pack.py.
depends-on: templates/header.yaml, content/02-output-contract.xml, scripts/validate-govtech-foia-ba-pack.py.
token-budget-impact: ~1500 tokens to fill end-to-end.
-->
---
version: 0.1.0
system_name: {{ system_name }}
jurisdiction: {{ jurisdiction }}
records_officer: {{ records_officer }}
access_request_officer: {{ access_request_officer }}
schedule_approved_on: {{ schedule_approved_on }}
launch_date: {{ launch_date }}
---

# System and jurisdiction

- system_name: {{ system_name }}
- jurisdiction: {{ jurisdiction }} (us-federal | us-state | uk | eu | ca-federal | ca-provincial)
- access_request_clock_working_days: <20 for us-federal and uk; confirm otherwise>

# Retention schedule

One row per record class (r-retention-schedule-per-record-class). Disposition is destroy or transfer-to-archives; never open-ended.

| Record class | Retention period (ISO-8601) | Disposition | Schedule item | Stores |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| <citizen submissions> | P7Y | destroy | <NARA GRS / agency / archives item> | <store names> |
| <audit logs> | P3Y | destroy | <item> | <store names> |

# Data stores and export paths

One row per store (r-request-export-within-statutory-clock). Lead time must sit inside the clock or the store is a blocking finding.

| Store | Export tool | Query | Owner (role:handle) | Lead time (working days) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| <store> | <tool> | <query> | role:<handle> | <n> |

# Exemption map

One row per withheld field (r-exempt-fields-tagged-in-schema). Manual-review rows carry a cost estimate.

| store.field | Category | Statutory basis | Redaction | Manual-review cost estimate |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| <store.field> | personal-privacy | <5 U.S.C. §552(b)(6) / UK FOIA s.40 / ...> | field-driven | — |

# Staff channels

Every channel staff use for business about the system (r-ephemeral-channels-captured).

| Channel | Capture mechanism | Auto-delete | Non-official copy within days (us-federal, max 20) |
|---|---|---|---|
| <channel> | <mechanism into the system of record> | false | — |

# Accessibility audit plan

- wcag_version: 2.1 | 2.2
- level: AA
- standard_reference: section-508 | en-301-549 | uk-psbar-2018 | aoda | other
- launch_gate: no-critical-or-serious-failure
- accessibility_statement_required: true | false
- accessibility_statement_url: <URL when required>

| Flow | Automated tool | Manual tests | Remediation owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| <public flow> | <axe-core / Lighthouse / ...> | screen-reader, keyboard-only, zoom-200 | role:<handle> |

# Procurement clause review log

One block per mandatory topic (r-procurement-clause-review-log): data_residency, security_authorisation, source_code_escrow_and_ip, open_source_licence, subcontractor_flow_down, accessibility_warranty, records_transfer_on_termination.

| Topic | Clause id | Design decision | Status | Waived by | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| data_residency | <clause id> | <decision it forces> | met | — | <URL> |

# Public notice

- assessed: true
- required: true | false
- regime: pra | state-apa | uk-consultation | eu-consultation | other
- buffer_days: <at least 90 plus review time when required>
- notices_filed: <60-day-federal-register YYYY-MM-DD; 30-day-federal-register YYYY-MM-DD; omb-submission YYYY-MM-DD>
- omb_control_number: <NNNN-NNNN when issued>

# Officers

- records_officer: {{ records_officer }}
- access_request_officer: {{ access_request_officer }}
- schedule_approved_on: {{ schedule_approved_on }}

# Launch

- launch_date: {{ launch_date }}

# Blocking findings

- <store past the clock, untagged exempt field, open clause, unscheduled notice period; or "none">
